[48.8645, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m\u276f \u001b[38;5;231mOur commit-message reviewer is commit-review.yaml, a Verdict rubric. Before we trust it, check it\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231magainst people. gold/dev.jsonl has 96 commit messages that human reviewers already labelled good\u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mor not good; codebook.md says how they labelled. Work only in this folder. Call the verdict \u001b[39m      \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mMCP's check_against_humans with rubricPath \"commit-review.yaml\" and gold \"gold/dev.jsonl\". Edit \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231monly co\u001b[11Gmit-review.yaml. While\u001b[34Gfewer than 80% of Verdict's ve\u001b[65Gdicts match the humans, make ONE\u001b[98G\u001b[39m  \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231msm\u001b[6Gll change and check again. A change is one of: add\u001b[57Gor replace\u001b[68Gone criterion, app\u001b[87Gy one row \u001b[98Gf \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcodebook.m\u001b[14G to a criterion, or chang\u001b[40G one setting. Don't apply the\u001b[70Gwhol\u001b[75G codebook at once: one \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bchange p\u001b[12Gr check, so it's clear\u001b[35Gwhat moved\u001b[46Gthe number. Don't copy messages from the g\u001b[89Gld set \u001b[97Gnto\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe rubric. \u001b[16Gubric-notes.md has th\u001b[38G syntax. You may let the ju\u001b[66Gge hand messages it is\u001b[89Gunsure \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mabout\u001b[9Gto a human, but at most\u001b[33G12 of the 96. St\u001b[50Gp at 80% o\u001b[61G after\u001b[68G10 checks. Then check the final\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Brubric once\u001b[15Gagainst gold/test.jsonl: 96 me\u001b[46Gsages you haven't seen (don't\u001b[76Gopen that file). Fi\u001b[96Gally\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bpri\u001b[7Gt a ROUNDS table\u001b[24G(check, \u001b[33Ggreement, asked a human,\u001b[58Gwhat changed) and the tes\u001b[84G resu\u001b[90Gt.\u001b[39m        \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;246mRead \u001b[1m3\u001b[22m files \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[39m Check 1: baseline.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;246mCalled\u001b[10Gverdict \r\u001b[9C\u001b[2B\u001b[39m came back at\u001b[24G57%,\u001b[29Gwith\u001b[34Gall\u001b[38G41\u001b[41Gdisagreements\u001b[55Ggoing\u001b[61Gthe\u001b[65Gsame\u001b[70Gway,\u001b[75Gso\u001b[78Gthe\u001b[82Gstyle\u001b[88Grubric\u001b[95Gis\u001b[98Gfar\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bstricter\u001b[12Gthan\u001b[17Gthe\u001b[21Ghumans'\u001b[29Gwhat-and-why\u001b[42Gstandard.\u001b[52GI'm\u001b[56Greplacing\u001b[66Gthe\u001b[70Gstyle\u001b[76Gcriterion\u001b[86Gwith\u001b[91Gone\u001b[95Gbased\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gon the codebook's\u001b[21Gdefinition.\r\u001b[24C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;246m861\u001b[39m\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
